# R&C Roofing — Visual Design System

> **Canonical reference:** `src/pages/index.astro` is the finished reference page. When in doubt, match it exactly.
> This rule is **project-specific** and must not be applied to any other project.

---

## Required Import

Every page should import `SectionBg` for consistent section backgrounds:

```astro
import SectionBg from '~/components/ui/SectionBg.astro';
```

The `SectionBg` component handles all background patterns internally — no need to import `simplePattern` directly.

Site-wide motif (shape, which sections, fade, tile size) lives in `src/config/motif.ts`. Colors and opacity live in `CustomStyles.astro`. Do not hardcode pattern SVGs on pages.

---

## Section Color Flow

Sections repeat in this order down every page. Never skip or reverse the order.

```
White → Grey (#FAFAFA) → Black → White → Grey → Black → … → Yellow (Final CTA)
```

---

## 1 · Hero Section (always White bg)

- Component: `Hero2` (left content / right image split)
- Background: white with yellow accent motif at **10% opacity**, top-to-bottom fade
- Left side: H1, subtitle paragraphs, primary CTA button
- Right side: hero image
- No eyebrow text. No gold bar. No `isDark`.
- **Do NOT add `tag-pill` badges unless they are explicitly listed in the content brief.** Omit `<Fragment slot="content">` entirely when badges are not provided.

```astro
<Hero2
  actions={[{ variant: 'primary', text: 'CTA Text', href: '/contact' }]}
  image={{ src: 'IMAGE_URL', alt: 'Alt text' }}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Page H1<br />Line Two</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="subtitle">
    First paragraph.
    <br /><br />
    Second paragraph.
  </Fragment>
  <!-- Only include the content slot when badges are explicitly given in the content brief -->
  <!-- <Fragment slot="content">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-6">
      <span class="tag-pill">Badge One</span>
    </div>
  </Fragment> -->
  <Fragment slot="bg">
    <SectionBg variant="hero" />
  </Fragment>
</Hero2>
```

---

## 2 · Grey Section Rules (`bg-[#FAFAFA]`)

- Background: always exactly `#FAFAFA`
- Headings: `text-heading`
- Body text: `text-muted`
- No motif
- **Cards are BLACK** — dark cards on a light grey background create intentional contrast

### Grey section bg snippet
```astro
<Fragment slot="bg">
  <SectionBg variant="grey" />
</Fragment>
```

### Card on Grey bg
```astro
<div class="rounded-lg border border-accent/60 bg-[#222] p-4 md:p-5 flex flex-col shadow-none outline-none">
  <h3 class="text-[16px] md:text-[18px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-2 text-white">{title}</h3>
  <p class="text-[13px] md:text-[14px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-white/60">{description}</p>
</div>
```

Optional left accent bar for compact cards: add `border-l-4 border-l-accent` to the card div.

### Ghost button on Grey bg

```astro
<a href="/path" class="btn-ghost-light">Button Label</a>
```

Or use the Button component:
```astro
<Button variant="ghost-light" text="Button Label" href="/path" />
```

### Step/numbered circle on Grey bg

When a step or process uses a numbered circle indicator, the circle must be dark with yellow text:

```astro
<div class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-full bg-[#222] flex items-center justify-center font-heading font-medium text-[15px] text-accent mt-0.5">
  {step}
</div>
```

- Circle bg: `bg-[#222]`
- Number text: `text-accent` (yellow)
- Never use `bg-primary`, `bg-white`, or any other colour for step circles on a grey background

---

## 3 · Black Section Rules (`bg-black` + motif)

- Background: `bg-black`
- Motif: `simple.svg` accent yellow at **12% opacity**, top-to-bottom fade
- Headings: `text-white`
- Body text: `text-white/70`
- Disclaimer / secondary text: `text-white/50`
- **Cards are dull black with yellow border**

### Black section bg snippet
```astro
<Fragment slot="bg">
  <SectionBg variant="dark" />
</Fragment>
```

### Card on Black bg
```astro
<div class="rounded-lg border border-accent/60 bg-[#222] p-6 flex flex-col">
  <h3 class="text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-3 text-white">{title}</h3>
  <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-white/60">{description}</p>
</div>
```

Use `isDark={true}` on `WidgetWrapper` for black sections. Pass `cardClass="border border-accent/60 bg-[#222]"` to `Features2` or `Testimonials` components.

### Ghost button on Black bg

```astro
<a href="/path" class="btn-ghost-dark">Button Label</a>
```

Or use the Button component:
```astro
<Button variant="ghost-dark" text="Button Label" href="/path" />
```

