## 5 · Final CTA Banner (always last section on every page)

- The `WidgetWrapper` section always sits on a **white background** (no bg override needed on the wrapper itself)
- The inner card: `bg-accent` (yellow) — **no border on the card**
- Motif: from `src/config/motif.ts` + `--aw-color-motif-cta` / `--aw-opacity-motif-cta` (R&C: black chevron at 3%). `CTABanner` applies it — do not paste mask CSS.
- Heading: `text-black`
- Body text: `text-black/70`
- Contact info: `text-black/70`, name bold `text-black`
- Separator: `border-t-2 border-black`
- CTA button: `bg-black text-white hover:bg-zinc-900`

```astro
<CTABanner title="CTA Heading" subtitle="Supporting sentence." />
```

---

## 6 · Testimonials Section

Testimonials follow the section color flow but have special rules when using black cards on grey backgrounds:

### Testimonials on Grey bg with black cards
When placing Testimonials on a grey section with black cards (`cardClass="border border-accent/60 bg-[#222]"`):
- Set `isDark={true}` — this makes card text (name, job, testimonial) white
- Override the headline with explicit dark text classes to keep the section title dark

```astro
<Testimonials
  title="Section Title"
  subtitle="Subtitle text"
  isDark={true}
  cardClass="border border-accent/60 bg-[#222]"
  classes={{ headline: { title: 'text-[26px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] text-[#111111]', subtitle: 'text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-[#444444]' } }}
  testimonials={[...]}
  callToAction={{
    variant: 'ghost-light',
    text: 'Button Text',
    href: '/path',
  }}
>
  <Fragment slot="bg">
    <SectionBg variant="grey" />
  </Fragment>
</Testimonials>
```

**Key rules:**
- `isDark={true}` for white text on black cards
- Explicit headline classes for dark section title on grey bg
- CTA button uses `variant: 'ghost-light'` (black text/border on grey)

